  "assign": {
    "_about": "Person -> body scores (gen_crowd.assign): a body must match the person's age band and sex, be in the community's `accepts` and not be used in the zone yet; robe bodies only wear Order roles and Order roles only robes. Among those: the build, the body's own community, a preferred kit; each earlier use costs `per_use`. Ties break by a seeded hash.",
    "build": 10.0, "home": 4.0, "accepted_rank": 0.5, "kit": 3.0, "per_use": 2.5,
    "tint_min_distance": 40.0,
    "tint_tries": 24
  },
  "clip_libraries": {
    "_about": "M3-CRE-662: the crowd bodies share the villager rig (one skeleton, the same bone names), so each group shares one AnimationLibrary (build_crowd.py build_library: assets/crowd/clips/crowd_<library>_clips.tres, built in `ref`'s job on its skeleton with the members' mean _persona and every member's work clips). The import (game/data/import/crowd.json `libraries`, the same map) gives every member its group's library and scales the hips track to its own height. Groups by measurement (tools/tests/test_npc.py SharedClips samples it): each member's own clips against the reference's played on it, world positions of the hands, feet, toes, knees and head over every clip. Within these groups the skeleton's part is at most 1.0 cm (feet height 0.4 cm); one library for all would be 4.7 cm (the small children) and flatten the elders' lean; the children split at the small pair (4.6 cm from the tall ones' reference).",
    "adult": {"ref": "crowd_man_medium_b", "bodies": ["crowd_man_heavy", "crowd_man_heavy_b", "crowd_man_lean_a", "crowd_man_lean_b", "crowd_man_medium_a", "crowd_man_medium_b", "crowd_order_man", "crowd_order_woman", "crowd_woman_heavy", "crowd_woman_lean_a", "crowd_woman_lean_b", "crowd_woman_medium", "crowd_woman_medium_b"]},
    "elder": {"ref": "crowd_elder_man_a", "bodies": ["crowd_elder_man_a", "crowd_elder_man_b", "crowd_elder_woman_a", "crowd_elder_woman_b"]},
    "child": {"ref": "crowd_girl_teen", "bodies": ["crowd_boy_tall", "crowd_girl_tall", "crowd_girl_teen"]},
    "child_small": {"ref": "crowd_boy_small", "bodies": ["crowd_boy_small", "crowd_girl_small"]}
  },
  "skin_clearance": {
    "_about": "M3-CRE-662: cloth never reads as bare skin. skin_delta_e (tools/validate_npc.py; gen_crowd.py draws with it and the validator checks it): CIE76 ΔE on CIELAB (D65) split into its lightness, chroma and hue parts, sqrt((k_l dL)^2 + dC^2 + (k_h dH)^2); k_l = k_h = 1 is CIE76 itself. k_l 0.3 and k_h 0.5 weigh the chroma step most: a warm low-chroma cloth (cream, sand, peach) reads as skin over a wide band of lightness and hue (a cream or sand top on mid-brown skin did, in M3-CRE-659's crowd_lineup_a, and a lighter cream on the same body still did in M3-CRE-662's first pass at k 0.75 / floor 24), while a grey (no chroma), white or a strong colour clears. Every cloth tint (a person's and a body's default _tints) must stand at least `floor` from the body's skin. A draw that misses is never kept: draw_cloth tries `tries` draws from the slot's own mixes, then as many from each of the community's other cloth sets (a, b, c), then each of the slot's swatches mixed toward `widen.dark` or `widen.light` (away from the skin's lightness first) by each of `widen.steps`, and stops with an error naming the person or body if none clears.",
    "k_l": 0.3,
    "k_h": 0.5,
    "floor": 18.5,
    "tries": 12,
    "widen": {"dark": "lacquer_black", "light": "gauze_white", "steps": [0.15, 0.3, 0.45, 0.6]},
    "calibration": {
      "_about": "How the weights and floor were picked; tools/tests/test_npc.py SkinClearance re-measures every entry. `pass`: palette swatches or hex that must clear the floor on every skin of the crowd's range (each community's two skin endpoints and their midpoint). `pass_pairs` / `fail_pairs`: [cloth, skin] that must clear / miss it. The fail pairs are what the renders showed reading as skin: the review's two pale tops in M3-CRE-659's crowd_lineup_a (man_heavy_b's cream #D1C0A1 on #AC7A5D, girl_tall's sand #BFAA86 on #A5765A) and the lighter cream #D7C9AF the first pass of this task gave man_heavy_b (it still read as skin); then peach and sand of the skin's hue and the skin-brown swatches at skin lightness. Measured at k_l 0.3, k_h 0.5: lowest pass order_marble on #C4977A 20.6 (salt_glass 21.3, faded_teal_cloth 21.5, gauze_white 22.5, the greys 25.4-26.7); highest fail the lighter cream on #AC7A5D 16.7 (the old cream 13.9, timber_weathered 13.2, laterite 13.0, girl_tall's sand 9.5, sand_cloth on #C4977A 6.7, tortoiseshell 4.5, peach 3.2-3.5, sand #C8A27E 2.5). The floor 18.5 sits mid-band (16.7-20.6), about 2 from each side; the widest band a grid over k_l in [0.2, 1] and k_h in [0.25, 2.5] finds. Plain CIE76 has none (thatch 13.5 below laterite 14.3; that cream on #AC7A5D is 31.3, far above the greys' 26). Consequence: creams and beiges fail near any crowd skin (cream #D1C0A1 on the dark #87593D is 16.3): they are drawn away to whites, greys and colours.",
      "pass": ["#5A5A5A", "#8A8A8A", "#B0B0B0", "gauze_white", "order_marble", "lacquer_black", "cold_blue_stone", "indigo_dye", "sea_blue_cloth", "faded_teal_cloth", "palm_green", "lacquer_red", "salt_glass"],
      "pass_pairs": [["bone", "#8A5A3E"], ["gold_leaf", "#B9876A"]],
      "fail_pairs": [["#D7C9AF", "#AC7A5D"], ["#D1C0A1", "#AC7A5D"], ["#BFAA86", "#A5765A"], ["#E2B496", "#C4977A"], ["#D9A585", "#B9876A"], ["#C8A27E", "#C4977A"], ["sand_cloth", "#C4977A"], ["tortoiseshell", "#74472E"], ["laterite", "#A06A4C"], ["timber_weathered", "#9A6A4E"]]
    }
  }
}
